(§ 259.5 Customer Service Plan.) Tj T*
(\(b\)\(5\) Providing prompt refunds in the original form of payment \(i.e., money is returned to an) Tj T*
(individual using whatever payment method the individual used to make the original payment, such) Tj T*
(as a check, credit card, debit card, cash, or airline miles\) when ticket or ancillary service) Tj T*
(fee refunds, including checked bag fee refunds, are due pursuant to 14 CFR part 260 unless the) Tj T*
(consumer agrees to receive the refunds in a different form of payment that is a cash equivalent) Tj T*
(payment as defined in 14 CFR 260.2. Carriers may not retain a processing fee for issuing refunds) Tj T*
(that are due;) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(§ 260.6 Refunding fare for flights cancelled or significantly delayed or changed by carriers.) Tj T*
(\(a\) Carriers' obligation to provide refunds—\(1\) Carriers' obligation. A covered carrier that is) Tj T*
(the merchant of record must provide a full and prompt refund of the airfare, including any taxes) Tj T*
(and ancillary fees, as set forth in paragraph \(a\)\(2\) of this section to a consumer that holds a) Tj T*
(nonrefundable ticket on a scheduled flight to, from, or within the United States for any) Tj T*
(cancelled flight or significantly delayed or changed flight where the consumer chooses not to:) Tj T*
(\(i\) Fly on the significantly delayed or changed flight or accept rebooking on an alternative) Tj T*
(flight; or \(ii\) Accept any voucher, credit, or other form of compensation offered by the air) Tj T*
(carrier or foreign air carrier pursuant to paragraph \(c\) of this section. \(2\) Automatic refunds.) Tj T*
(A full refund of the airfare, including any taxes and ancillary fees, is due to a consumer as) Tj T*
(described in paragraphs \(a\)\(2\)\(i\) through \(iii\) of this section: \(i\) A flight is canceled and a) Tj T*
(consumer is not offered an alternative flight or any voucher, credit, or other form of) Tj T*
(compensation by the air carrier or foreign air carrier pursuant to paragraph \(c\) of this) Tj T*
(section; \(ii\) A consumer rejects the significantly delayed or changed flight, rebooking on an) Tj T*
(alternative flight, or any voucher, credit, or other form of compensation offered by the covered) Tj T*
(carrier pursuant to paragraph \(c\) of this section; or \(iii\) A consumer does not respond to an) Tj T*
(offer of: \(A\) A significantly delayed or changed flight or an alternative flight and the flight) Tj T*
(departs without the consumer; or \(B\) A voucher, credit, or other form of compensation by the) Tj T*
(date on which the cancelled flight was scheduled to depart or the date that the significantly) Tj T*
(delayed or changed flight departs.) Tj T*
(\(b\) Individuals with a disability. A carrier that is the merchant of record must provide a full) Tj T*
(and prompt refund to an individual with a disability upon notification by the individual with a) Tj T*
(disability that he/she does not want to continue travel because of the significant changes) Tj T*
(described in paragraphs \(b\)\(1\) through \(3\) of this section. The covered carrier must also) Tj T*
(provide a full and prompt refund to any individuals in the same reservation as the individual) Tj T*
(with a disability who do not want to continue travel without the individual with a disability in) Tj T*
(situations described in paragraphs \(b\)\(1\) through \(3\). \(1\) The individual with a disability is) Tj T*
(downgraded to a lower class of service that results in one or more accessibility features needed) Tj T*
(by the individual becoming unavailable. \(2\) The individual with a disability is scheduled to) Tj T*
(travel through one or more connecting airports that are different from the original itinerary.) Tj T*
(\(3\) The individual with a disability is scheduled to travel on a substitute aircraft on which) Tj T*
(one or more accessibility features available on the original aircraft needed by the individual) Tj T*
(are unavailable.) Tj T*
(\(c\) Alternative to refund. A covered carrier may offer a voucher, credit, or other form of) Tj T*
(compensation as an explicit alternative to providing a refund required by paragraph \(a\) of this) Tj T*
(section if: \(1\) The offer includes a clear and conspicuous notice of— \(i\) The terms of the offer) Tj T*
(as specified in § 260.8; and \(ii\) The consumer's right to a full refund under this section. \(2\)) Tj T*
(The voucher, credit, or other form of compensation offered explicitly as an alternative to) Tj T*
(providing a refund required by paragraph \(a\) of this section remains valid and redeemable by the) Tj T*
(consumer for a period of at least five years from the date on which such voucher, credit, or) Tj T*
(other form of compensation is issued; \(3\) Upon the issuance of such voucher, credit, or other) Tj T*
(form of compensation, a covered carrier notifies the recipient of the expiration date of the) Tj T*
(voucher, credit, or other form of compensation; and \(4\) Upon request by an individual who self) Tj T*
(identifies as an individual with a disability a covered carrier provides a notification under) Tj T*
(paragraph \(c\)\(3\) of this section in an electronic format accessible to the recipient.) Tj T*
(\(d\) Carriers' obligation to notify ticket agents. In situations where a ticket agent is the) Tj T*
(merchant of record for the transaction, after receiving a refund request by a consumer through) Tj T*
(the ticket agent, the carrier that canceled or significantly delayed or changed the flight must) Tj T*
(inform the ticket agent without delay whether the consumer is eligible for a refund under this) Tj T*
(section \(i.e., whether the consumer has accepted the significantly changed flight, the) Tj T*
(alternative flight, or other compensation offered in lieu of refunds\).) Tj T*
(\(e\) Carriers' obligation to transfer funds to ticket agents. In situations where a ticket agent) Tj T*
(is responsible for providing the refund to the consumer pursuant to 14 CFR 399.80\(l\) and the) Tj T*
(ticket agent does not possess the funds of the consumer, that carrier that has the funds must) Tj T*
(promptly transfer the funds to the ticket agent.) Tj T*
